00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:45.840
They keep their contracts. They keep their profits. They just point one percent of their death machines at actual death.

110
00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:53.780
This isn't just about saving lives; it's about potentially creating the biggest growth industry of the century: the business

111
00:11:53.780 --> 00:12:01.380
of not-dying. What Happens If This Actually Works. The Endgame: Reorienting Global Priorities.

112
00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.690
A one percent treaty isn't the goal. It's the proof of concept.

113
00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:13.780
I've watched roughly ten thousand civilizations reach this exact fork in the road; the ones still around all started with

114
00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:18.540
something like one percent, and the ones that didn't are geological features now.

115
00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:26.260
Once your species gets a taste of "spending money on things that help instead of things that explode," you'll want more.

116
00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:31.460
You're not appealing to better angels. You're making peace more profitable than war.

117
00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:37.020
Turns out humans will do anything if you pay them enough, including surviving.

118
00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:42.080
The Ratchet Effect: How to Boil a Frog (The Frog is the War Machine).

119
00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:50.560
Once a one percent treaty is signed and the first cures for "untreatable" diseases start rolling out, the system becomes

120
00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:54.940
more valuable. Every five to ten years, you hold another global vote.

121
00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:59.320
"Hey, that worked out great. Grandma's dementia is manageable now.

122
00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.990
You stopped that pandemic before it started. Want to try another half-percent?".

123
00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:11.660
More cures lead to more popular support, which leads to more votes for more funding, which leads to more cures.

124
00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:20.140
It's a self-reinforcing flywheel for peace. The endgame: countries bragging about their cancer survival rates instead of

125
00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:28.840
their missile counts. For quantitative projections of health and economic impacts, see impact dot war on disease dot org.

126
00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.720
Avoiding Treaty Pitfalls. Treaties fail in predictable ways.

127
00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:41.960
I know because I've catalogued every failed treaty on every planet I've consulted for, and they all fail for the same five

128
00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:48.240
boring reasons. Here's how this one avoids the common killers: Reservation Games.

129
00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:52.740
Countries love to sign treaties then add exceptions that gut them.

130
00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:57.120
It's like joining a gym but reserving the right to never go.

131
00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:02.260
Solution: No reservations permitted. All or nothing. Take it or leave it.

132
00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:10.020
Ratification Delays. Sign with fanfare, take a photo, then let it die in committee forever.

133
00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:16.120
Your species calls this "diplomacy.". Solution: Provisional application.

134
00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:21.120
Takes effect on signature. Ratification just formalizes what already started.

135
00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:31.280
Creative Accounting. Reclassify "military" spending as "peacekeeping" or "homeland security" to dodge obligations.

136
00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:39.760
Solution: Incentive Alignment Bonds, or I.A.B.s, make creative accounting self-defeating.

137
00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:47.840
Politicians who benefit from treaty compliance have personal financial incentive to ensure their nation's full one percent

138
00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:56.080
contribution flows through. Reclassifying military spending to dodge obligations reduces I.A.B.

139
00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:01.550
returns for that nation's own legislators, the same people who control budget classifications.

140
00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:08.360
Parliamentary Obstacles. Executive signs, legislature refuses to implement.

141
00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:17.940
Solution: The treaty obligates the percentage; Congress implements via the annual National Defense Authorization Act (N.D.A.A.).

142
00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:27.340
After Medellin v. Texas (two thousand and eight), the U.S. Supreme Court made clear that not all treaties are self-executing,

143
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:32.740
and a treaty directing budget appropriations would collide with Congress's power of the purse.

144
00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:41.340
So the treaty doesn't try to bypass Congress. It creates a binding international obligation that Congress fulfills through

145
00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:46.140
its normal appropriations process, the same way NATO's spending commitments work.

146
00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:55.380
The I.A.B. mechanism ensures legislators have a personal financial incentive to include the one percent line item every

147
00:15:55.380 --> 00:16:02.740
year. In other signatory nations, similar provisions route implementation through existing budget processes.

148
00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:12.840
Summary. A one percent treaty is a piece of paper that says "Let's spend one percent less on killing and one percent more

149
00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:18.260
on not dying.". That's it. That's the whole thing. It doesn't end war.

150
00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:22.100
It doesn't destroy the military. It doesn't create world peace.

151
00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:28.100
It just moves the *first* one percent of your murder budget to your survival budget.

152
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:36.060
If you can't agree on that, if you can't agree that spending one penny less on death and one penny more on life is a good

153
00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:42.880
idea, then you deserve whatever's coming. Addendum: The Actual Treaty Text (First Draft).

154
00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:51.100
THE TREATY FOR THE one percent REALLOCATION OF MILITARY EXPENDITURES TOWARDS BIOMEDICAL RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT FOR THE

155
00:16:51.100 --> 00:17:01.000
PREVENTION OF HUMAN SUFFERING AND DEATH (Or: The "Let's Not Die" Treaty, for short) WHEREAS, humanity spends two point seven

156
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:10.640
two trillion dollars annually on methods of killing itself; WHEREAS, this seems somewhat counterproductive; WHEREAS, diseases

157
00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:19.079
kill more people than all wars combined and don't even have the decency to be quick about it; WHEREAS, we have nuclear weapons

158
00:17:19.079 --> 00:17:30.280
sufficient to end civilization thirteen times but haven't cured Alzheimer's once; WHEREAS, this is embarrassing; NOW, THEREFORE,

159
00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:39.460
the undersigned nations agree to stop being complete idiots about this, as follows: Article One: Each signatory shall redirect

160
00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:49.010
exactly one percent of its annual military budget to the one percent Treaty Fund for allocation to pragmatic clinical trials.

161
00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:54.640
Article Two: Transfers shall be automatic, immediate, and irrevocable.

162
00:17:54.720 --> 00:18:01.300
No "we'll get to it later." Article Three: Percentages may increase but never decrease.

163
00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:09.180
This is a ratchet, not a yo-yo. Article Four: Compliance shall be verified by blockchain and A.I.

164
00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:19.900
No creative accounting. Article Five: Non-compliant parties lose access to incentive-alignment bonds, or I.A.B.

165
00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:25.520
benefits, and treaty fund advantages. Your opponents get what you forfeit.

166
00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:30.720
Article Six: Success metrics trigger mandatory percentage reviews.

167
00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:38.920
When it works, we do more. Article Seven: Citizens have standing to enforce via domestic courts.

168
00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:47.780
You can sue your own government for non-compliance. Article Eight: Withdrawal requires unanimous consent of all parties

169
00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:57.220
plus ten-year notice. Good luck with that. Article Nine: This treaty supersedes all conflicting domestic law.

170
00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:03.880
Yes, even that law. Article Ten: Entry into force upon signature by two states.

171
00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:12.160
You only need two countries brave enough to go first. IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the undersigned, being of sound mind and tired

172
00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:17.520
of watching their loved ones die of preventable diseases, have executed this Treaty.

173
00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:22.450
Signed this day, blank, in the year of our ongoing confusion.

174
00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:29.840
[Nation Name]. "We choose life, I guess". P.S. - Yes, this includes space weapons.

175
00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:30.900
Nice try.
